A scoped support package is a directory containing `@package.moth`. The directory supplies its package name.

[codeblock, $code "text":
    @entry.moth
    blog/
    ├── @package.moth
    └── helpers/dates.moth
]

`@blog` is visible to the entry root and eligible normal sibling modules.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @blog post_title
]

Only declarations marked by `$export` in `blog/@package.moth` are public. Support roots can re-export selected helpers but do not create pages.

A project-root `@package.moth` is the external project package surface. Internal project modules cannot import it. See @#project-local-packages (Project-local packages).
